+
+/*
+  Her garden: the greeting in Indian time, her own seeded bed with the Naira
+  flower planted the day she joined and her stone flower beside it, one honest
+  card, and "What's growing", which is also the garden in words for a screen
+  reader (the drawing itself is decorative). The dates in her gift ledger
+  bloom on the arbour, a small stone flower each in its month's colour; each
+  order the shop confirmed grows a gold-leaf rose in the front row, dated
+  with it (after the Doors, in a chunk of its own); the Naira flower's pieces
+  she has taken home from her rooms stand at the arbour's crown (Phase 6). On her first signed-in visit, and
